    "notes": "F10. Six actual action stages each facing: approach right wrist blades to left shield, contact the shield seen in thin metallic edge profile, clack/compress, separate, deliberately expose/open guard with the same two blades, return. Root and producer review accept contact on the visible metal thickness of the rim, rather than imposing a particular orange paint pixel. The roots of the right blades are occluded by the open right palm in the exposed pose, remain aligned with the same gauntlet and are visible before/after; no extra hand or detached weapon is introduced. Correct anatomical LEFT shield and RIGHT blades persist. Native alpha2 gutters and all selected cells are safe. This is authored BODY choreography only: no sound event, taunt AI effect or combat opening mechanic implemented. Fixed reviewed MASK-crown-to-soles reference excludes hair and weapons. Independent final QA agreed with this contact/occlusion reading and approved both complete pages; contradictory earlier concerns are preserved in the intake ledger. Calibrations are excluded; playback durations are for visual inspection, not source mechanics."
